---
title: Two-bean Vegetable Goulash
author: Shirley Simmonds
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 1 hour 20 minutes
---

Drain the @black beans{100%g}(soaked overnight) and @cannellini beanrs{100%g}(soaked overnight) rinse them under cold running water. Put them in a #pan{} and cover with water. Bring to the boil and boil fast for ~{10%minutes}. Then lower the heat, half cover the pans and simmer for about ~{60%minutes} until tender. Drain, rinse and set aside.

Heat the @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} in a large #pan{} with a lid and fry the @shallots{100%g}(peeled and left whole), @celery{4}(scrubbed and sliced into chunks), @courgettes{4}(cut into 2.5cm chunks) and @carrots{3}(scrubbed and cut lengthways into chunks) quickly over high heat until lightly browned.

Pour in the @tomatoes{1%can} with their juice and the @vegetable stock{300%ml}. Stir in the @paprika{1%tbsp}, @caraway seeds{1/2%tsp}, @salt{}, and freshly ground @black pepper{}. Cover the pan and simmer for ~{20%minutes} until the vegetables are tender.

Stir both lots of beans into the vegetables. Blend the @cornflour{1%tbsp} with @water{2%tbsp} and add to the pan. Bring to the boil, stirring gently until the sauce thickens a little. Cover the pan and simmer again for about ~{10%minutes}.

Spoon the goulash into a warm dish and serve with @?soured cream{150%ml} if liked.

> The goulash can be prepared up to 24 hours in advance and kept tightly covered in the fridge. Reheat gently in a large pan for ~{15%minutes}.
